    <pageContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a58b29f0-29c6-47b8-b8ce-329b38fbed3c",
      "key": "c06daed5-c427-4f35-be25-0c55c96b769a",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch2\u003EThe challenge\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Centre for Legal Leadership (CLL) is a unique professional community for the Global in-house legal community. CLL were keen to improve the findability and discoverability of their high-value knowledge content, which was often buried within the site structure and effectively hidden.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBy increasing the visibility of articles and viewpoints, they aimed to increase the number of repeat visitors to the website and attract new in-house professionals, helping to build the CLL community and brand.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe CLL team came to us with a brief to make it easier to spotlight new articles and viewpoints, allow visitors to browse through the knowledge article collection on different themes and enhance the search. In parallel, they also wanted to enhance the site\u0027s design to make sure it was eye-catching but also easy to use.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cblockquote\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0022Our website is a critical channel for CLL, and our knowledge content is a core part of our value proposition for the in-house legal community. The new website features help to make that content far more visible. The combination of 3Chillies\u0027s expertise in Sitecore development, Konstructive\u0027s strong design work and some excellent communication during the project have really enhanced the site.\u0022 \u2014 Rebecca Cater, Head of the Centre for Legal Leadership, RPC\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/blockquote\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe work we delivered\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWorking closely with the CLL team and design partners Konstructive, we held two workshops to define and prioritise the client\u0027s requirements in more detail. From this, we were able to scope the project while Konstructive worked on designs for several new page templates and components. Following sign-off from the client, we developed and deployed the new capabilities and designs in CLL\u0027s existing Sitecore instance.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe results\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA new knowledge landing page allows the CLL team to curate and spotlight knowledge articles on different themes, with a variety of presentation options to pique visual interest. A new embedded search facility on each knowledge page allows keyword-driven and contextual searching through the knowledge collection. The overall site search has been dramatically improved, with the card format extended to present search results for all content types.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe CLL team are very pleased with the new site designs, and feedback from the in-house legal community has been highly positive, remarking on the improved visibility of knowledge content. The refreshed website is going from strength to strength, continuing to attract visits from right across the in-house community while encouraging a stream of content contributions from prominent GCs and experts.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
